IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc24-ministerial-review`

-- ccc24-tests-ministerial-review.l4 -- tests for ccc24-ministerial-review.l4 (Criminal Code ss 696.1 to 696.87).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section, row by row, before the run.  T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING.

§ `Part XXI.1 -- sections 696.1 to 696.6`

-- 696.1(1): arguments are (convicted, found a dangerous or long-term offender, rights exhausted).
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a dangerous offender finding
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- rights of appeal not exhausted
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither convicted nor found
#ASSERT `s 696.1(1) an application for ministerial review on the grounds of miscarriage of justice may be made to the Minister of Justice` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.1(2) the application is in the form, contains the information and is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.1(2) the application is in the form, contains the information and is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- points to the regulations
#ASSERT `s 696.1(2) the application is in the form, contains the information and is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.1(2) the application is in the form, contains the information and is accompanied by the documents prescribed by the regulations` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) the Minister of Justice must review the application in accordance with the regulations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(1) the Minister of Justice must review the application in accordance with the regulations` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "On receipt of an application"
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) the Minister of Justice has and may exercise the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act and the powers that may be conferred on a commissioner under section 11 of that Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.2(2) the Minister of Justice has and may exercise the powers of a commissioner under Part I of the Inquiries Act and the powers that may be conferred on a commissioner under section 11 of that Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a member of the bar
#ASSERT `s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a retired judge
#ASSERT `s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- another individual in the Minister's opinion
#ASSERT `s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- none of the three kinds
#ASSERT `s 696.2(3) the Minister of Justice may delegate the Minister's powers to take evidence, issue subpoenas, enforce the attendance of witnesses, compel them to give evidence and otherwise conduct an investigation under subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in writing

#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) court of appeal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) court of appeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the keel's section 2 answer (a "means" definition: JUST FALSE) is carried through
#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) court of appeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(1) court of appeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not the court of the province of the trial
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) the Minister of Justice may refer a question to the court of appeal for its opinion` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) the Minister of Justice may refer a question to the court of appeal for its opinion` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) the Minister of Justice may refer a question to the court of appeal for its opinion` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) the court of appeal must furnish its opinion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(2) the court of appeal must furnish its opinion` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

`ccc24 fixture 696a` MEANS `s 696.3(3)(a)(i) direct a new trial before any court that the Minister thinks proper`
`ccc24 fixture 696b` MEANS `s 696.3(3)(a)(i) direct a new hearing under Part XXIV`
`ccc24 fixture 696c` MEANS `s 696.3(3)(a)(ii) refer the matter to the court of appeal for hearing and determination as if it were an appeal`
`ccc24 fixture 696d` MEANS `s 696.3(3)(b) dismiss the application`
`ccc24 fixture 696x` MEANS `s 696.3(3) another step`

-- 696.3(3): arguments are (the step, an application is before the Minister, satisfied there is a reasonable basis, found a dangerous or long-term offender).
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696a` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(i) a new trial
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696a` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied: "if the Minister is satisfied"
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696b` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a new hearing for a dangerous offender
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696b` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a new hearing is only for a person found to be a dangerous or long-term offender
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696c` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696c` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696d` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) dismiss, needing no satisfaction
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696d` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no application is before the Minister
#ASSERT `s 696.3(3) the Minister of Justice may take the step on the application` `ccc24 fixture 696x` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.3(4) the decision of the Minister of Justice is final and is not subject to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.3(4) the decision of the Minister of Justice is final and is not subject to appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a decision of another kind: the text is silent

`ccc24 fixture 696m1` MEANS `s 696.4(a) whether the application is supported by new matters of significance that were not considered by the courts or previously considered by the Minister`
`ccc24 fixture 696m2` MEANS `s 696.4(b) the relevance and reliability of information that is presented in connection with the application`
`ccc24 fixture 696m3` MEANS `s 696.4(c) the fact that an application is not intended to serve as a further appeal and any remedy available on it is an extraordinary remedy`
`ccc24 fixture 696mx` MEANS `s 696.4 another matter`

#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696m1` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696m2` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696m3` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696m1` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a decision under 696.3(3)
#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696mx` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "all matters that the Minister considers relevant"
#ASSERT `s 696.4 the Minister of Justice must take the matter into account` `ccc24 fixture 696mx` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a matter the Minister does not consider relevant
#ASSERT `s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the last day of the sixth month
#ASSERT `s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` TRUE 3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- late: the period is fixed
#ASSERT `s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` FALSE 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- still not submitted after the period
#ASSERT `s 696.5 the Minister of Justice submitted the annual report in time` FALSE 3 EQUALS NOTHING   -- not yet due: the text is silent

-- 696.5 as a regulative rule: a submission at month 6 is FULFILLED; a lapse to month 7 is a BREACH.  Compared across both stable builds.
#TRACE `s 696.5 the annual report rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister of Justice` DOES `s 696.5 submit the annual report to Parliament` AT 6

#TRACE `s 696.5 the annual report rule` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 7)

§ `Part XXI.2 -- sections 696.7 to 696.87`

#ASSERT `s 696.7 applicant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.7 applicant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a "means" definition
#ASSERT `s 696.7 Commission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.7 Commission` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.7 Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.7 Minister` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 3 of the Milgaard Act not yet in force
#ASSERT `s 696.72(a) the Commission's mandate is to review the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.72(b) the Commission's mandate is to make a recommendation to a relevant public authority or body` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.72(b) the Commission's mandate is to make a recommendation to a relevant public authority or body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.72(b) the Commission's mandate is to make a recommendation to a relevant public authority or body` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "must", not "no"
#ASSERT `s 696.8 the Commission has ensured that the person is able to communicate readily with the Commission from any place in Canada` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person who is neither an applicant nor a potential applicant
#ASSERT `s 696.81 the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website and has provided the public with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.81 the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website and has provided the public with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.81 the Commission has published information about its mandate on its website and has provided the public with information about its mandate and about miscarriages of justice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.82(1) the Commission carries out its mandate in a transparent manner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.82(1) the Commission carries out its mandate in a transparent manner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.82(2) the Commission has published its decisions on its website in the manner the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.82(2) the Commission has published its decisions on its website in the manner the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a decision that does not protect confidential information
#ASSERT `s 696.82(2) the Commission has published its decisions on its website in the manner the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.82(2) the Commission has published its decisions on its website in the manner the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.83(1) the Commission may adopt the policy` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(1) the Commission may adopt the policy` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.83(3) the Commission has published its policies on its website` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(3) the Commission has published its policies on its website` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.83(4) the Statutory Instruments Act applies to the policy` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not apply"
#ASSERT `s 696.83(4) the Statutory Instruments Act applies to the policy` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a policy that the Commission did not adopt: not covered
#ASSERT `s 696.85 the Commission and its employees have followed established procedures and practices for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.85 the Commission and its employees have followed established procedures and practices for the secure handling, storage, transportation and transmission of information or documents` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 6832a` MEANS `s 696.83(2)(a) the making of applications`
`ccc24 fixture 6832b` MEANS `s 696.83(2)(b) each stage of the review process`
`ccc24 fixture 6832c` MEANS `s 696.83(2)(c) applications that are made on behalf of persons`
`ccc24 fixture 6832d` MEANS `s 696.83(2)(d) the provision of notices and other information to applicants, to their representatives, to attorneys general and to other interested persons, including victims`
`ccc24 fixture 6832e` MEANS `s 696.83(2)(e) meetings of the Commission`
`ccc24 fixture 6832x` MEANS `s 696.83(2) another subject`

#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832a` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832b` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832c` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832d` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832e` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.83(2) the Commission must adopt policies respecting the subject` `ccc24 fixture 6832x` EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 6841a` MEANS `s 696.84(1)(a) direct employees to provide applicants and potential applicants with general information and guidance on applications and each stage of the review process`
`ccc24 fixture 6841a1` MEANS `s 696.84(1)(a.1) direct employees to notify the Correctional Service of Canada and the Parole Board of Canada of the importance of ensuring that applicants and potential applicants do not experience barriers`
`ccc24 fixture 6841b` MEANS `s 696.84(1)(b) enter into contracts in its own name`
`ccc24 fixture 6841c` MEANS `s 696.84(1)(c) provide supports to applicants in need`
`ccc24 fixture 6841d` MEANS `s 696.84(1)(d) enter into contracts with persons who have technical or specialized knowledge to assist in the Commission's work`
`ccc24 fixture 6841x` MEANS `s 696.84(1) another power`

-- 696.84(1): arguments are (the power, carrying out its mandate, supports are for an applicant in need, the contract is with a person with technical knowledge).
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841a` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841a1` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841b` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841c` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841c` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- supports to a person who is not an applicant in need
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841d` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841d` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841b` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not carrying out its mandate
#ASSERT `s 696.84(1) the Commission may exercise the power in carrying out its mandate` `ccc24 fixture 6841x` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

`ccc24 fixture 6842a` MEANS `s 696.84(2)(a) directing them to services in their communities for persons in need or helping them access those services`
`ccc24 fixture 6842b` MEANS `s 696.84(2)(b) providing them with translation and interpretation services`
`ccc24 fixture 6842c` MEANS `s 696.84(2)(c) assisting them in relation to necessities such as food and housing`
`ccc24 fixture 6842d` MEANS `s 696.84(2)(d) assisting them in obtaining legal assistance in relation to making an application or providing a written response to an investigation report prepared by the Commission`
`ccc24 fixture 6842x` MEANS `s 696.84(2) another support`

#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842a` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842b` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842c` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842c` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "if they are without means"
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842d` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842d` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842a` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an applicant in need
#ASSERT `s 696.84(2) the support is a support to applicants in need` `ccc24 fixture 6842x` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "include": the list is not closed

